  data: {
    LLM: '1. Building the Tableau: You can move cards within the tableau to build sequences in alternating colors (e.g., a Black 7 on a Red 8).\n2. Foundations: Move Aces to the foundations as soon as they become available. Build foundations UP by suit (A-2-3...K).\n3. The Stock: Flip cards from the stock (usually 3 at a time) to find moves. In some variations, you can only go through the stock once.',
    Player: '1. Building the Tableau: You can move cards within the tableau to build sequences in alternating colors (e.g., a Black 7 on a Red 8).\n2. Foundations: Move Aces to the foundations as soon as they become available. Build foundations UP by suit (A-2-3...K).\n3. The Stock: Flip cards from the stock (usually 3 at a time) to find moves. In some variations, you can only go through the stock once.',
    objective: 'Move all 104 cards to the 8 foundation piles (2 for each suit), building each suit from Ace to King.',
    gameplay: '1. Building the Tableau: You can move cards within the tableau to build sequences in alternating colors (e.g., a Black 7 on a Red 8).\n2. Foundations: Move Aces to the foundations as soon as they become available. Build foundations UP by suit (A-2-3...K).\n3. The Stock: Flip cards from the stock (usually 3 at a time) to find moves. In some variations, you can only go through the stock once.',
    keyRules: [
      'Only a King (or a sequence starting with a King) can be moved into an empty tableau space.',
      'Whole sequences can be moved as long as the bottom card follows the alternating-color rule for the target column.',
      'There are 8 foundation slots; each suit must be completed twice.',
